# The Book — local environment example. Copy to `.env` and fill in the values for
# your NON-PRODUCTION Supabase project. Never commit your real `.env` (it is
# gitignored).
#
# Both values below are PUBLIC client configuration:
#   - EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is the project URL.
#   - EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is the anon key. It is RLS-gated and is meant
#     to be embedded in the client bundle, so it is not a secret.
# Anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the app bundle by Expo and must
# be treated as public.
#
# DO NOT put the Supabase service-role key (or any private secret) here or in any
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable — it would be bundled into the client. The service-role
# key is only used by tooling/seed scripts via a private, non-EXPO env var
# (SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY / TEST_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY) — see
# .env.tooling.example.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
